{"id": "EUVD-2026-101231", "enisaUuid": "24e2d5e4-38db-3d48-baa9-fac78eaf634b", "description": "LASzip through 3.5.0 contains an invalid free vulnerability in laszip_read_header() that allows attackers to free uninitialized heap pointers via truncated variable length record data. Attackers can supply a crafted LAS/LAZ file with an inflated VLR count that, when opened and destroyed through the C API, crashes the process and corrupts the heap.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:16:44", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/LASzip/LASzip/commit/c9bfd3e68d65c84d513a2286ae06cbbe17afda02", "https://github.com/LASzip/LASzip/blob/3.5.0/src/laszip_dll.cpp#L3967-L3995", "https://github.com/LASzip/LASzip/blob/3.5.0/src/laszip_dll.cpp#L497-L511", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/laszip-vlr-uninitialized-free", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/laszip-through-3.5.0-invalid-free-via-truncated-vlr-header-in-laszip-read-header"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m6xh-mjq9-hv5w", "CVE-2026-110603"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a68496c0-2545-30df-ab6d-869f364764e4", "product": {"name": "LASzip", "vendor": {"name": "rapidlasso"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7d8f3b92-19ae-3d45-8342-85e9fae6af63", "vendor": {"name": "rapidlasso"}}], "isExploited": false}